{"format":"bench-library","formatVersion":1,"id":"clock-ds3231","name":"Real-time clock (DS3231)","version":"1.0.0","author":"Bench Workshop","owner":"codeopen0-cpu","description":"The DS3231 clock module: it keeps the date and time (starting from this PC's clock when the run starts, and running with the simulation: pausing pauses it) and has a thermometer. I2C at 0x68 (the same as an MPU-6050: they can't share a bus). Includes RTClib.h.","category":"Sensors","needsApp":"0.3.0","code":"// DS3231: registers 0x00 seconds, 0x01 minutes, 0x02 hours (24 h), 0x03 day of week (1-7),\r\n// 0x04 date, 0x05 month (bit 7: century), 0x06 year (00-99), all in BCD; 0x0E control (bits 3-4 square\r\n// wave rate, bit 2 INTCN), 0x0F status (bit 7: the clock stopped: lost power), 0x11-0x12 temperature\r\n// (whole degrees, then quarters in the top two bits).\r\nconst bcd = (n) => ((Math.floor(n / 10) << 4) | (n % 10)) & 255;\r\nconst unbcd = (b) => (b >> 4) * 10 + (b & 15);\r\n\r\nbench.device('ds3231', (part) => {\r\n  const temp = part.control('temp');\r\n  const cell = part.params.cell !== false;\r\n  // the time it keeps: seconds since 1970 (as local time) at simulation time `at`\r\n  let base = Math.floor(Date.now() / 1000) - new Date().getTimezoneOffset() * 60 + Number(part.params.offset ?? 0) * 60;\r\n  let at = 0, now = 0;\r\n  const regs = new Array(19).fill(0);\r\n  regs[0x0e] = 0x1c;\r\n  regs[0x0f] = cell ? 0x00 : 0x80; // (no cell: it \"lost power\" and has to be set)\r\n  let powered = false, ptr = 0, reads = 0, sets = 0, setTo = null;\r\n  const secondsNow = () => base + Math.floor(now - at);\r\n  const fill = () => {\r\n    const d = new Date(secondsNow() * 1000);\r\n    regs[0] = bcd(d.getUTCSeconds()); regs[1] = bcd(d.getUTCMinutes()); regs[2] = bcd(d.getUTCHours());\r\n    regs[3] = d.getUTCDay() + 1; regs[4] = bcd(d.getUTCDate()); regs[5] = bcd(d.getUTCMonth() + 1) | (d.getUTCFullYear() >= 2100 ? 0x80 : 0);\r\n    regs[6] = bcd(d.getUTCFullYear() % 100);\r\n    const t = Math.round(temp.value * 4);\r\n    regs[0x11] = (Math.floor(t / 4)) & 255; regs[0x12] = (t & 3) << 6;\r\n  };\r\n  return {\r\n    i2c: {\r\n      address: () => (powered ? 0x68 : -1),\r\n      write(bytes) {\r\n        if (!bytes.length) return true;\r\n        ptr = bytes[0] % 19;\r\n        let timeSet = false;\r\n        for (let i = 1; i < bytes.length; i++) {\r\n          const r = (ptr + i - 1) % 19;\r\n          regs[r] = bytes[i];\r\n          if (r <= 6) timeSet = true;\r\n          // (writing the status with bit 7 clear clears \"lost power\")\r\n        }\r\n        if (timeSet) {\r\n          // the program set the time: from now on it counts from what was written\r\n          const y = 2000 + unbcd(regs[6]) + (regs[5] & 0x80 ? 100 : 0);\r\n          base = Date.UTC(y, unbcd(regs[5] & 0x1f) - 1, unbcd(regs[4]), unbcd(regs[2] & 0x3f), unbcd(regs[1]), unbcd(regs[0] & 0x7f)) / 1000;\r\n          at = now;\r\n          regs[0x0f] &= 0x7f;\r\n          sets++;\r\n          setTo = new Date(base * 1000).toISOString().replace('T', ' ').slice(0, 19);\r\n        }\r\n        return true;\r\n      },\r\n      read(n) {\r\n        reads++;\r\n        fill();\r\n        const out = [];\r\n        for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) out.push(regs[(ptr + i) % 19]);\r\n        ptr = (ptr + n) % 19;\r\n        return out;\r\n      },\r\n    },\r\n    step(io) {\r\n      now = io.time;\r\n      const v = io.supply('VCC', 'GND');\r\n      powered = v >= 2.3;\r\n      // (on its coin cell it keeps time even unpowered; without one it stops, and says so)\r\n      if (!powered && !cell) { base = secondsNow(); at = now; regs[0x0f] |= 0x80; }\r\n      if (!powered) { io.release('SQW'); io.draw(0); return; }\r\n      const sqwOn = !(regs[0x0e] & 0x04);\r\n      if (sqwOn) io.drive('SQW', (now % 1) < 0.5 ? v : 0, 1);\r\n      else io.drive('SQW', v, 0); // (INTCN: open drain, idle high through its pull-up)\r\n      io.draw(0.0002);\r\n    },\r\n    status() {\r\n      if (!powered) return [cell ? 'no power (keeping time on its coin cell)' : 'no power'];\r\n      const d = new Date(secondsNow() * 1000).toISOString().replace('T', ' ').slice(0, 19);\r\n      return [`${d}${regs[0x0f] & 0x80 ? ' (lost power: not set)' : ''}, ${temp.value} C`, `${reads} reads${sets ? `, set to ${setTo}` : ''}`];\r\n    },\r\n  };\r\n});\r\n","sketch":{"RTClib.h":{"classes":["RTC_DS3231","RTC_DS1307","DateTime","TimeSpan"],"exports":["__DATE__","__TIME__","F","DS3231_SquareWave1Hz","DS3231_OFF"],"code":"// RTClib.h (Adafruit's): RTC_DS3231 rtc;  rtc.begin();  DateTime now = rtc.now();\n//   now.year(), month(), day(), hour(), minute(), second(), dayOfTheWeek() (0 = Sunday), unixtime();\n//   rtc.adjust(DateTime(F(__DATE__), F(__TIME__)));  rtc.lostPower();  rtc.getTemperature();\n//   DateTime(2026, 11, 15, 19, 30, 0);  now + TimeSpan(1, 0, 0, 0) (a day later)\nconst F = (s) => s;\nconst MONTHS = ['Jan', 'Feb', 'Mar', 'Apr', 'May', 'Jun', 'Jul', 'Aug', 'Sep', 'Oct', 'Nov', 'Dec'];\nconst _built = new Date();\nconst __DATE__ = `${MONTHS[_built.getMonth()]} ${String(_built.getDate()).padStart(2, ' ')} ${_built.getFullYear()}`;\nconst __TIME__ = [_built.getHours(), _built.getMinutes(), _built.getSeconds()].map((n) => String(n).padStart(2, '0')).join(':');\nconst DS3231_OFF = 0x1c, DS3231_SquareWave1Hz = 0x00;\nconst _bcd = (n) => ((Math.floor(n / 10) << 4) | (n % 10)) & 255;\nconst _unbcd = (b) => (b >> 4) * 10 + (b & 15);\n\nclass TimeSpan {\n  constructor(days = 0, hours = 0, minutes = 0, seconds = 0) {\n    this.secs = arguments.length === 1 ? days : days * 86400 + hours * 3600 + minutes * 60 + seconds;\n  }\n  days() { return Math.trunc(this.secs / 86400); }\n  hours() { return Math.trunc(this.secs / 3600) % 24; }\n  minutes() { return Math.trunc(this.secs / 60) % 60; }\n  seconds() { return this.secs % 60; }\n  totalseconds() { return this.secs; }\n}\n\nclass DateTime {\n  /** DateTime(unixtime) / DateTime(y, m, d, h, mi, s) / DateTime(\"Nov 15 2026\", \"19:30:00\") / DateTime(other) */\n  constructor(a = 946684800, m, d = 1, h = 0, mi = 0, s = 0) {\n    if (a instanceof DateTime) this.t = a.t;\n    else if (typeof a === 'string') {\n      const [mon, day, year] = a.trim().split(/\\s+/);\n      const [hh, mm, ss] = String(m ?? '00:00:00').split(':').map(Number);\n      this.t = Date.UTC(Number(year), Math.max(0, MONTHS.indexOf(mon)), Number(day), hh, mm, ss) / 1000;\n    } else if (m === undefined) this.t = Number(a);\n    else this.t = Date.UTC(a < 100 ? 2000 + a : a, m - 1, d, h, mi, s) / 1000;\n  }\n  _d() { return new Date(this.t * 1000); }\n  year() { return this._d().getUTCFullYear(); }\n  month() { return this._d().getUTCMonth() + 1; }\n  day() { return this._d().getUTCDate(); }\n  hour() { return this._d().getUTCHours(); }\n  twelveHour() { const h = this.hour() % 12; return h === 0 ? 12 : h; }\n  isPM() { return this.hour() >= 12; }\n  minute() { return this._d().getUTCMinutes(); }\n  second() { return this._d().getUTCSeconds(); }\n  dayOfTheWeek() { return this._d().getUTCDay(); }\n  unixtime() { return this.t; }\n  secondstime() { return this.t - 946684800; }\n  isValid() { return Number.isFinite(this.t); }\n  /** \"YYYY-MM-DDThh:mm:ss\" (or the buffer's own pattern: \"hh:mm:ss\", \"DD/MM/YYYY\") */\n  timestamp(opt = 0) {\n    const iso = this._d().toISOString().slice(0, 19);\n    return opt === 1 ? iso.slice(11) : opt === 2 ? iso.slice(0, 10) : iso;\n  }\n  toString(fmt) {\n    if (typeof fmt !== 'string') return this.timestamp();\n    const p = (n, w = 2) => String(n).padStart(w, '0');\n    return fmt.replace('YYYY', p(this.year(), 4)).replace('YY', p(this.year() % 100)).replace('MM', p(this.month())).replace('DD', p(this.day()))\n      .replace('hh', p(this.hour())).replace('mm', p(this.minute())).replace('ss', p(this.second())).replace('DDD', ['Sun', 'Mon', 'Tue', 'Wed', 'Thu', 'Fri', 'Sat'][this.dayOfTheWeek()]);\n  }\n  add(span) { return new DateTime(this.t + (span instanceof TimeSpan ? span.secs : Number(span))); }\n  sub(x) { return x instanceof DateTime ? new TimeSpan(this.t - x.t) : new DateTime(this.t - (x instanceof TimeSpan ? x.secs : Number(x))); }\n}\nDateTime.TIMESTAMP_FULL = 0;\nDateTime.TIMESTAMP_TIME = 1;\nDateTime.TIMESTAMP_DATE = 2;\n\nclass RTC_DS3231 {\n  constructor() { this.addr = 0x68; }\n  _r(reg, n) {\n    Wire.beginTransmission(this.addr); Wire.write(reg);\n    if (Wire.endTransmission() !== 0) return null;\n    if (Wire.requestFrom(this.addr, n) < n) return null;\n    const out = [];\n    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) out.push(Wire.read());\n    return out;\n  }\n  _w(reg, bytes) { Wire.beginTransmission(this.addr); Wire.write(reg); for (const b of bytes) Wire.write(b); return Wire.endTransmission() === 0; }\n  begin() { Wire.begin(); return this._r(0x0f, 1) !== null; }\n  lostPower() { const s = this._r(0x0f, 1); return !!s && !!(s[0] & 0x80); }\n  now() {\n    const r = this._r(0x00, 7);\n    if (!r) return new DateTime(0);\n    return new DateTime(2000 + _unbcd(r[6]) + (r[5] & 0x80 ? 100 : 0), _unbcd(r[5] & 0x1f), _unbcd(r[4]), _unbcd(r[2] & 0x3f), _unbcd(r[1]), _unbcd(r[0] & 0x7f));\n  }\n  adjust(dt) {\n    const d = dt instanceof DateTime ? dt : new DateTime(dt);\n    this._w(0x00, [_bcd(d.second()), _bcd(d.minute()), _bcd(d.hour()), d.dayOfTheWeek() + 1, _bcd(d.day()), _bcd(d.month()) | (d.year() >= 2100 ? 0x80 : 0), _bcd(d.year() % 100)]);\n    const s = this._r(0x0f, 1);\n    if (s) this._w(0x0f, [s[0] & 0x7f]);\n  }\n  getTemperature() { const r = this._r(0x11, 2); return r ? (r[0] >= 128 ? r[0] - 256 : r[0]) + (r[1] >> 6) * 0.25 : NAN; }\n  writeSqwPinMode(mode) { this._w(0x0e, [mode]); }\n  readSqwPinMode() { const r = this._r(0x0e, 1); return r ? r[0] & 0x1c : 0; }\n}\nclass RTC_DS1307 extends RTC_DS3231 {\n  isrunning() { return !this.lostPower(); }\n}\n"}},"parts":[{"id":"ds3231","name":"Clock (DS3231 module)","description":"Keeps the time with its coin cell, even with the board off. VCC (3.3-5 V), GND, SDA, SCL (SQW: a 1 Hz square wave if asked). #include <RTClib.h>; RTC_DS3231 rtc; rtc.begin(); DateTime now = rtc.now(); now.hour()... Set it once with rtc.adjust(DateTime(F(__DATE__), F(__TIME__)));","swatch":"#1d4fb8","mass":8,"params":[{"key":"cell","label":"Coin cell fitted","kind":"bool"},{"key":"offset","label":"Its time is off by (minutes)","kind":"number","min":-100000,"max":100000,"step":1}],"defaults":{"cell":true,"offset":0},"shape":[{"box":[3.8,0.16,2.2],"at":[0,0.08,0],"color":"#1d4fb8"},{"box":[0.8,0.2,0.8],"at":[-0.6,0.26,0.2],"color":"#141416"},{"cyl":[0.85,0.35],"at":[0.9,0.34,0.15],"color":"#c9cdd4"}],"pinRows":[{"ids":["32K","SQW","SCL","SDA","VCC","GND"],"at":[-1.85,0,-0.635],"dir":"z","kinds":{"32K":"out","SQW":"out","SCL":"i2c","SDA":"i2c","VCC":"vin","GND":"gnd"},"extra":{"VCC":{"label":"VCC (3.3-5 V)","vmin":2.3,"vmax":5.5}}}],"controls":[{"id":"temp","kind":"slider","label":"Room temperature (C)","min":-20,"max":60,"step":0.25,"value":22}],"device":"ds3231"}],"examples":[{"name":"Clock and thermometer","description":"A board reads the clock every second and prints the date, the time and the temperature. Press Run and open the board's serial monitor.","project":{"format":"bench-workshop","version":1,"name":"Clock and thermometer","parts":[{"uid":"board","type":"maker-board","name":"Board","params":{"usb":true},"parent":null,"pos":[-8,0,0],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"rtc","type":"clock-ds3231/ds3231","name":"Clock","params":{},"parent":null,"pos":[5,0,0],"rot":[0,0,0,1]}],"wires":[{"id":"w1","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"3V3"},"b":{"uid":"rtc","pin":"VCC"},"color":"#e04848"},{"id":"w2","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GND"},"b":{"uid":"rtc","pin":"GND"},"color":"#2b2d33"},{"id":"w3","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"SDA"},"b":{"uid":"rtc","pin":"SDA"},"color":"#3cb371"},{"id":"w4","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"SCL"},"b":{"uid":"rtc","pin":"SCL"},"color":"#f2f2f2"}],"programs":{"board":{"lang":"arduino","source":"// Clock and thermometer: the DS3231 keeps the date and time; this prints them every second.\n#include <Wire.h>\n#include <RTClib.h>\n\nRTC_DS3231 rtc;\nchar daysOfTheWeek[7][12] = {\"Sunday\", \"Monday\", \"Tuesday\", \"Wednesday\", \"Thursday\", \"Friday\", \"Saturday\"};\n\nvoid print2(int n) {   // two digits: 7 -> 07\n  if (n < 10) Serial.print('0');\n  Serial.print(n, DEC);\n}\n\nvoid setup() {\n  Serial.begin(115200);\n  if (!rtc.begin()) {\n    Serial.println(\"No DS3231: check its wires\");\n    while (true) delay(100);\n  }\n  if (rtc.lostPower()) {\n    Serial.println(\"The clock lost power: setting it to when this sketch was built\");\n    rtc.adjust(DateTime(F(__DATE__), F(__TIME__)));\n  }\n}\n\nvoid loop() {\n  DateTime now = rtc.now();\n  Serial.print(daysOfTheWeek[now.dayOfTheWeek()]);\n  Serial.print(\" \");\n  Serial.print(now.year(), DEC);\n  Serial.print(\"-\");\n  print2(now.month());\n  Serial.print(\"-\");\n  print2(now.day());\n  Serial.print(\"  \");\n  print2(now.hour());\n  Serial.print(\":\");\n  print2(now.minute());\n  Serial.print(\":\");\n  print2(now.second());\n  Serial.print(\"   \");\n  Serial.print(rtc.getTemperature());\n  Serial.println(\" C\");\n  delay(1000);\n}\n"}},"boards":[]}}]}